[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Implemented complete pretense module with 5-section architecture: (1) TargetState dataclass modeling DAG/WaveScheduler/DAGRunner state with 20+ transitions, (2) make_target_fakes factory synthesizing state-machine fakes, (3) TestTargetUnit with 15 fake-based unit tests verifying transitions and error contracts, (4) TestTargetImplReal with 35+ real-implementation tests achieving full coverage of DAG operations, scheduler policies (FAIL_FAST, CONTINUE_ON_ERROR, SKIP_DOWNSTREAM), and runner lifecycle, (5) Hypothesis TargetFuzzTest compiled from proto for property-based equivalence verification.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite.py: Implemented DAG engine interface module with service protocols (DAG, WaveScheduler, DAGRunner) and data types (NodeDefinition, NodeResult, DAGRunReport, DAGError, CycleError, NodeNotFoundError, NodeExecutionError) matching low/dag_engine_lite.pyi specification.
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/lib/dag_engine_lite_impl.py: Implemented concrete DAG, WaveScheduler, and DAGRunner singletons with full DAG operations (add/remove nodes, edges, validation, cycle detection, topological sort, critical path), wave scheduling, failure policy handling, retry logic, and sequential DAG execution producing DAGRunReport.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: In add_edge.returns (lines 160-168), the function returns _as_outcome(outcome) without first validating that both upstream_id and downstream_id exist in state.nodes, violating dag_engine_lite.pyi line 187 which mandates 'WHEN upstream_id or downstream_id does not exist, MUST raise NodeNotFoundError'; the returns handler must check node existence and raise NodeNotFoundError when either identifier is absent from state.nodes.
[BLAME] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: In mark_succeeded.provide (lines 581-593), the function only promotes dependents already present in state.scheduler_states, but add_node.provide (lines 114-142) never initializes new nodes into state.scheduler_states, so newly added dependents like node 'b' are never initialized as PENDING or READY; this violates dag_engine_lite.pyi line 398-399 which mandates 'MUST evaluate downstream dependents and promote newly unblocked nodes to READY' since untracked dependents are silently skipped; fix requires add_node.provide to initialize every new node into scheduler_states (READY for roots, PENDING for dependents).
[CHANGE] benchmark_1/parts/dag_engine_lite/pretense/dag_engine_lite_impl_pretense.py: Fixed two feedback items: (1) add_edge.returns now validates both upstream_id and downstream_id exist in state.nodes before returning, raising NodeNotFoundError per dag_engine_lite.pyi line 187 contract; (2) add_node.provide now initializes every new node in scheduler_states (READY for root nodes with no dependencies, PENDING for nodes with dependencies), ensuring mark_succeeded.provide can properly evaluate downstream dependents and promote newly unblocked nodes to READY.
